*~
/@fvdycore
/fvdycore
/fvdycore@
/@gtFV3
/gtFV3
/gtFV3@
__pycache__
build_cuda_r4/
build_cuda_r8/
# Local diagnostic / benchmark scratch files
*_3a11*.sh
*_3a11*.out
*_3a11*.txt

# Specific local diagnostic directories
dt3a11v/

# Slurm / debug output
*.out

# Any out-of-source CUDA build tree, not just the two named above. The perf
# benchmark lives in build_cuda_r8_perf/ (it is behind BUILD_FV3_GPU_PERF_BENCH
# and is deliberately absent from the r8/r4 trees), and further variants are
# cheap to create, so match the prefix rather than enumerating.
build_cuda_*/

# Slurm job output and compute-sanitizer / diagnostic logs. These are produced in
# the repository root by the GPU legs, are large, and are never source.
slurm-*.out
*.log
*.stdout
*.sorted

# Milestone 6A.5: converted authoritative grid-metric binaries are derived
# data (regenerable from the Fortran spgrid_* export via
# tools/grid_metrics/convert_fortran_grid_metrics.py), not source. Keep the
# converter and its test committed; keep the *.bin/manifest.json output out.
tools/grid_metrics/c8_authoritative/

# Milestone 6A.5 Section 10: converted SP0 dynamical-state binaries
# (tools/savepoints/convert_sp0_to_cuda.py output) and CUDA device-readback
# dumps (run_small_perf_bench.cpp --sp0-dump output) are derived/generated
# data, not source. Keep the converter and comparator scripts committed;
# keep the *.bin/manifest.json output out.
tools/savepoints/sp0_cuda_authoritative/
tools/savepoints/sp0_cuda_dump_*/
tools/savepoints/sp0_cuda_sentinel_test/
